      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Morse code is a universal language used to send messages through pulses
    of light or sound.\n\nEvery letter in the alphabet is made up of a unique combination
    of just two simple signals:\n\n-The Dot ( . ) \u2014 A short, quick pulse.\n\n-The
    Dash ( - ) \u2014 A longer pulse. A dash is exactly three times as long as a
    dot.\n\nBy combining dots and dashes into sequences, you get different letters,
    and subsequently words. For example, \"Morse Code\" is: -- --- .-. ... . / -.-.
    --- -.. .\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
